{
  "name": "422. BFL FLUX 3 Video: create, query, download, refusals, cancel (bfl flux 3 video)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6617 (contract C4 to C7, C9; BFL vendor sheet B15 to B19) on the unified video routes. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The config points bfl at the fixture's /pp/bfl, which answers POST /v1/flux-3-video with task bfl-video-ready and GET /v1/get_result by task id. Row 2 creates a task and reads the task object: queued, an id {vendor id}:bfl, the credit cost; row 3 reads the bytes BFL received: seconds as duration, 1080p as fhd, mode t2v, an extra field merged unchanged, no unified name left. Row 4 queries it: completed, the MP4 link in videos[], expires_at two hours after BFL's end_time. Row 5 queries a moderated task: failed with content_filter. Rows 6 to 8 are refused with caller_unsupported_parameter before any upstream call: callback_url and client_reference_id (FLUX 3 Video has no webhook_url or external id), size (BFL has no size). Row 9 is the cancel route: 400 provider_cancel_unsupported. Row 10 reads the fixture: one create and one query of each task. Before the change every bfl video request answered unsupported_operation. Every status, the dropped-connection once-only create and the download path are pinned by core/providers/bfl's Go tests.",
